> >What happens when someone who ate a black
> >dragon corpse pray in Genhennom or gets hit with black dragon breath?
>
> Well:
> >* Half disintegration resistance will cause disintegration attacks to
> > only halve your HP.
> ...instead of killing you.
> Although, that may be misleading - what it really does is make the
> disintegration attack hit you for (Max HP / 2) damage. So if your HP is
> below 50%, you die.

I forgot about the disintegration effect thing, sorry.  I think this
might be too difficult, since disintegration is, again, only available
in two ways, both black-dragon-related.  Eat the corpse, and you get
half protection.  Wear the armor, and get full protection.  Other than
that, reflection is the only real defense against black dragon breath.

I think my real problem here is that I think you're trying to solve a
problem that doesn't exist.  The problem isn't that *all* resistances
need to have lesser levels of strength, but that some pieces of
equipment are largely useless, while others are incredibly valuable.
For things like disintegration resistance, I'd consider leaving
vanilla's behavior intact.  For things like fire, cold, sleep, poison,
etc, I think your patch will probably be an improvement.

By the way, sorry to pick it apart like this, I'm not trying to be
antagonistic, really.  Just talking through some of the design issues
point by point, because I think it might help you (you can bet the
DevTeam will be thinking about all these things if they consider your
patch for inclusion)... and because I just like thinking about game
design.  Heh.

